fix(engine): preserve proved evidence across deduplication

Deduplicate accumulated only endpoints, references, Confidence and Source
order-invariantly. Reachable, ProvenPath, RouteConfirmed, TaintChain, Route and
SourceTier rode along with whichever member won findingLess — endpoint, then
evidence, then fix, then line, lexicographic.

So a confirmed SSRF at "z/views.py:674" merged with an unconfirmed duplicate at
"a/util.py:10" came out with Reachable=false, no taint chain, no bound route and
the semgrep tier. decision.corroborate reads exactly those fields, so dedup
could silently demote a genuinely confirmed finding to WARN.

This was NOT an arrival-order race. findingLess picks the same winner for every
permutation, so the erasure was systematic — the lexicographically-first
occurrence always won regardless of what it had proved. The new regression test
fails identically on both input orderings, which is how that was established.

These six fields live in the RENDER BLOCK, so evidence.ProvenanceIndex could
never have covered them: it exists to carry the Evidence-INTERNAL half across
the ToFinding projection, and its own invariant comment scopes it that way. The
gap was structural, not an omission.

They now fold by proof union — OR for the flags, max-trust for the tier,
prefer-the-member-that-proved-it for the chain and route. Only members that
CARRIED the evidence contribute, so the fold cannot manufacture it
(TestDedupDoesNotManufactureEvidence), and each operation is commutative,
associative and idempotent, so the merged finding stays a pure function of the
member set (TestDedupProofUnionIsOrderIndependent walks all six permutations of
a three-member group; F-L6).

This extends to the render block the same distinction mergeScoringProvenance
already documents for its own fields: agree-or-drop describes the NATURE of each
occurrence, proof-union preserves a positive fact about the logical
vulnerability that one occurrence established.

Full suite: 39 packages ok, 0 failures. Determinism suites pass at -count=3.

Refs RC-3.

